## Model card

- **Name:** MAI-Thinking-1
- **Short description:** Microsoft AI’s MAI-Thinking-1 is presented as an in-house reasoning model for complex problem solving/software engineering, emphasizing expert reasoning with cost-efficient serving (per official Microsoft AI model page).
- **Provider / access:** Microsoft AI (official model page/playground context). No public API model ID or public rate card found in accessible sources in this pass. Local metadata lists `microsoft/mai-thinking-1`, `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Official Microsoft AI model page reviewed 2026-11-14; technical paper/PDF linked from page (`/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/main_20260602_2.pdf` in page content) but not text-extractable in this pass. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in accessible reviewed content.
- **IDs:** `mai-thinking-1`, `MAI-Thinking-1`, `microsoft/mai-thinking-1`.
- **Context window:** 256,000 tokens (256K); max output 25,000 tokens (local metadata claim; not clearly extractable from accessible official page text in this pass).
- **Modalities:** Text input/output (per local metadata/positioning).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** No public token pricing/rate card published in accessible official sources in this pass (Microsoft page indicates cost-efficiency messaging but no concrete per-token rates). Local metadata pricing figures are unverified.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary closed model. Local metadata claims ~1T/35B-active MoE; accessible official page text in this pass did not provide a clearly extractable architecture/spec table to independently verify this claim.

